2. Platform-independent: The current code is specific to Unix-based systems. To make it platform-independent, we need to abstract the network communication logic from the underlying operating system. We can use a cross-platform library like Boost.Asio or libcurl for networking.
3. XML-based: We can make the data exchange format XML-based by using XML messages instead of plain text. We can use libraries like TinyXML or RapidXML for parsing XML messages.
