 To automatically prefix a string before using it as a regular expression in various programming languages, you can concatenate the prefix with the regex pattern. Here's an example using JavaScript:

```javascript
const prefix = 'autoPrefix';
const regexPattern = /pattern/; // your existing regex pattern
const completeRegexPattern = new RegExp(`^${prefix}${regexPattern.source}`);

