```

In this example, `prefix` is the string that you want to add before the regex pattern. The `^` symbol at the beginning of the regex pattern represents the start of the line anchor. This ensures that only strings starting with the prefix followed by the regex pattern will match.

You can also use this approach in other programming languages like Python, Ruby, or any other language that supports regular expressions. Just replace the syntax according to the specific language's regular expression library.

